ckly", "Research more", "Feel guilty", "Rationalize", "Talk to someone"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_18", "type": "choice", "label": "How much do you weigh future people (you’ll never meet) in decisions that affect this topic today?", "options": ["A lot", "Some", "Unsure how to", "Rarely", "Not consciously"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_19", "type": "choice", "label": "When brands or leaders speak on this topic, what erodes your trust fastest?", "options": ["Vague virtue signaling", "Data overreach", "Hypocrisy", "Fear messaging", "Overpromising"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_20", "type": "choice", "label": "If you could only protect one—honesty, kindness, or effectiveness—which do you lean on when they conflict here?", "options": ["Honesty", "Kindness", "Effectiveness", "Refuse to rank", "Situational blend"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_21", "type": "choice", "label": "Do you experience this topic more as a private inner struggle or a public political fight?", "options": ["Mostly private", "More private", "Both equally", "More public", "Mostly public"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_22", "type": "choice", "label": "How often do you update your views based on new evidence vs. doubling down?", "options": ["Update often", "Sometimes update", "Slow to update", "Rarely update", "Depends on the source"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_23", "type": "choice", "label": "Which risk worries you more in this area: being exploited, or missing an opportunity to help?", "options": ["Being exploited", "Missing help", "Both equally", "Neither—different fears", "Not sure"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_24", "type": "choice", "label": "When you feel powerless here, what do you usually do with that feeling?", "options": ["Channel it into action", "Numb or distract", "Talk it through", "Blame systems", "Sit with it quietly"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_25", "type": "choice", "label": "Would you rather be remembered as principled or pragmatic on this topic?", "options": ["Principled", "Pragmatic", "Both—contextual", "Neither matters to me", "I don’t think in those terms"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_26", "type": "choice", "label": "How much does your answer depend on where you live (country, city, infrastructure)?", "options": ["Completely", "Quite a bit", "Moderately", "Somewhat", "Hardly"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_27", "type": "choice", "label": "If your 18-year-old self disagreed with your current view, who would you listen to harder?", "options": ["Younger self (idealism)", "Current self (experience)", "Neither—merge the tension", "I can’t imagine", "Depends on the issue"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_28", "type": "choice", "label": "When you see others suffer in this domain, how often do you feel complicit in systems you participate in?", "options": ["Often", "Sometimes", "Rarely", "I reject guilt framing", "I oscillate"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_29", "type": "choice", "label": "Pick the tension that feels most alive for you right now:", "options": ["Freedom vs. safety", "Speed vs. care", "Truth vs. harmony", "Growth vs. limits", "Individual vs. collective"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_30", "type": "choice", "label": "How do you react when someone uses moral language (‘you should’) about this topic?", "options": ["Open if empathetic", "Defensive", "Curious about their story", "Dismissive if preachy", "Depends who says it"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_31", "type": "choice", "label": "If you had to teach a 20-minute class on this topic, what would you refuse to oversimplify?", "options": ["Causes", "Tradeoffs", "Who is hurt", "Solutions", "History"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_32", "type": "choice", "label": "Which lens do you trust least when people analyze this topic?", "options": ["Pure economics", "Pure morality", "Pure tech optimism", "Pure nostalgia", "Pure outrage"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_33", "type": "text", "label": "Name one assumption people make about ‘people like you’ in this topic that is often wrong or incomplete."}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_34", "type": "text", "label": "What is a constructive disagreement you wish more people could have about this—without collapsing into teams?"}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_35", "type": "text", "label": "If you could ask one question to the most powerful decision-maker in this space, what would it be—and why?"}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_36", "type": "text", "label": "What would you want researchers to measure that they rarely measure today?"}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_37", "type": "text", "label": "Describe a time you changed your behavior here—not because you were shamed, but because something clicked."}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_38", "type": "text", "label": "What is one thing you wish institutions (employers, schools, governments) understood about everyday lived experience here?"}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_39", "type": "choice", "label": "After reflecting, how clear is your own position on this topic?", "options": ["Very clear", "Somewhat clear", "Mixed", "Uncertain", "Intentionally open"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_40", "type": "choice", "label": "Would you want a close friend to challenge you on this more often, less often, or about the same?", "options": ["More often", "About the same", "Less often", "Depends on how they do it", "Not sure"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_41", "type": "choice", "label": "How likely are you to seek new information on this in the next month?", "options": ["Very likely", "Likely", "Maybe", "Unlikely", "Very unlikely"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_42", "type": "choice", "label": "Do you feel more hopeful, more concerned, or about the same compared to a year ago?", "options": ["More hopeful", "About the same", "More concerned", "Both hopeful and concerned", "I avoid comparing"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_43", "type": "choice", "label": "If you could fund one type of project in this area, what would you pick?", "options": ["Education", "Infrastructure", "Research", "Direct aid", "Advocacy"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_44", "type": "choice", "label": "How much does community (online or offline) matter for how you think about this topic?", "options": ["Essential", "Important", "Moderate", "Minor", "I think alone"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_45", "type": "choice", "label": "Would you rather improve your own situation first, or work on collective change first?", "options": ["Own situation", "Collective change", "Both in parallel", "Refuse the split", "Context-dependent"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_46", "type": "choice", "label": "How often do you translate reflection into concrete next steps?", "options": ["Often", "Sometimes", "Rarely", "I resist planning", "I over-plan"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_47", "type": "choice", "label": "What would make you disengage entirely from caring about this topic?", "options": ["Burnout", "Cynicism", "Competing priorities", "I can’t imagine", "Already happened sometimes"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_48", "type": "choice", "label": "How much do you want decision-makers to read honest, nuanced survey answers like yours?", "options": ["A lot—please share themes", "Some—aggregate only", "Little—privacy first", "Unsure", "No—too risky"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_49", "type": "choice", "label": "Does thinking this through leave you with more compassion, more urgency, or more ambivalence?", "options": ["More compassion", "More urgency", "More ambivalence", "Mix of all three", "Something else"]}, {"id": "platinumenvintergenerati_50", "type": "choice", "label": "Final calibration: how representative do you think your answers are of people in situations very different from yours?", "options": ["Very representative", "Somewhat", "Not very", "I doubt it", "I actively don’t know"]}]$json$::jsonb,
  true,
  'Environment',
  pc.id
from public.payment_categories pc
where pc.slug = 'platinum'
limit 1
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

